    <bpmn:process id="W_W805" name="W805. Workers&#x27; Compensation, SSS/ECC Claims &amp; Return-to-Work Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Workplace injury or illness reported per W140; or occupational disease detected per W804
Frequency: Ad-hoc; estimated 50-100 workplace injuries/year across 200 stores and 4 DCs (mostly minor)
Volume: ~1–3 SSS sickness benefit claims/month (the multi-day-confinement subset of the 50–100 mostly-minor injuries/year); ~2–5 ECC (Employees&#x27; Compensation Commission) claims/year for work-related injury/illness
Owner: HR Benefits Officer
Participants: Injured Employee, Store/DC Manager, Safety Officer, Occupational Health Physician, SSS, ECC, HR Manager, Department Head
Source: workflow W805 — Workers&#x27; Compensation, SSS/ECC Claims &amp; Return-to-Work Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W805_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W805_Lane1" name="Safety Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W805_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W805_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W805_Lane2" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W805_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W805_Lane3" name="HR Benefits Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W805_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W805_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W805_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W805_Lane4" name="Occupational Health Physician">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W805_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W805_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W805_Start6" name="Workplace injury or illness reported per W140; or occupational disease detected per W804">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W805_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W805_Task7" name="Immediate Injury Response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Immediate Injury Response: When workplace injury occurs: (a) first aid administered per W501; (b) if emergency: transport to nearest hospital; (c) incident reported per W140 within 24 hours; (d) Safety Officer conducts initial investigation; (e) Store/DC Manager notifies HR Benefits Officer within 24 hours; (f) HR confirms if injury is work-related based on incident report and circumstances
Responsible (R): Safety Officer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): HR Benefits Officer
Duration: Within 24 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W805_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W805_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W805_Task8" name="Medical Treatment &amp; Documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Medical Treatment &amp; Documentation: (a) employee receives medical treatment at company-designated clinic or nearest hospital; (b) attending physician completes Medical Certificate with: diagnosis, treatment plan, estimated recovery period, work restrictions; (c) for injuries requiring &gt;3 days absence: physician issues SSS sickness notification; (d) HR Benefits Officer collects all medical documentation; (e) for serious injuries: Occupational Health Physician coordinates ongoing medical management
Responsible (R): Employee / Occupational Health Physician
Accountable (A): HR Benefits Officer
Duration: 1-7 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W805_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W805_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W805_Task9" name="SSS Sickness Benefit Filing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: SSS Sickness Benefit Filing: For work-related absence &gt;3 days: (a) HR Benefits Officer files SSS Sickness Benefit claim: SSS sickness notification form, medical certificate, employer certification of salary deduction; (b) SSS processes claim and pays daily sickness allowance (90% of average daily salary credit) directly to employee; (c) BuildRight advances sickness allowance to employee within salary period and recovers from SSS; (d) claim processing time: 30-60 days
Responsible (R): HR Benefits Officer
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 3-5 days filing + 30-60 days SSS processing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W805_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W805_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W805_Task10" name="ECC Claim Filing (Serious Injury/Illness)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: ECC Claim Filing (Serious Injury/Illness): For serious work-related injury or occupational disease: (a) HR Benefits Officer files ECC claim under PD 626: ECC claim form, incident report per W140, medical certificates, SSS sickness benefit documentation; (b) ECC provides additional benefits: income benefit, medical reimbursement, rehabilitation services, carer&#x27;s allowance; (c) ECC claim processing: 60-90 days; (d) if claim denied: VP Legal assists with appeal to ECC
Responsible (R): HR Benefits Officer / VP Legal
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 5-10 days filing + 60-90 days ECC processing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W805_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W805_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W805_Task11" name="Return-to-Work Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Return-to-Work Processing: When employee is medically cleared: (a) Occupational Health Physician issues Return-to-Work Certificate with any restrictions (light duty, restricted lifting, modified hours); (b) HR coordinates with Department Head for work accommodation; (c) if restrictions apply: modified duty assignment for recovery period (typically 1-4 weeks); (d) if permanent partial disability: assess reasonable accommodation per Magna Carta; (e) if unable to return to any role: coordinate with SSS for disability benefit and process separation per W43
Responsible (R): Occupational Health Physician / HR / Department Head
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 1-5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W805_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W805_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W805_Task12" name="Incident Trend Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Incident Trend Analysis: Monthly, HR Benefits Officer and Safety Officer review workers&#x27; compensation data: (a) injury frequency rate by location, department, and cause; (b) lost workdays by injury type; (c) SSS/ECC claim costs; (d) repeat injury locations or roles; (e) findings feed into W512 store-level safety committee and W141 safety inspection programs; (f) quarterly report to CHRO and COO
Responsible (R): HR Benefits Officer / Safety Officer
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2-3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W805_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W805_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W805_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W805_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W805_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-313 (ensure controlled execution — Occupational Health &amp; Safety (PA-24.1).) | - operational: HR Benefits Officer review and approval gate
Owner: HR Benefits Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
