    <bpmn:process id="W_W1266" name="W1266. Store-Level Customer Safety Incident Management, First Aid Response &amp; Liability Documentation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Ad-hoc — triggered by any customer injury, illness, or safety incident occurring on BuildRight Depot premises (sales floor, lumber yard, parking area, receiving dock)
Frequency: As-needed; estimated 30–50 customer safety incidents per month chain-wide (minor: slips, falls, minor cuts; major: fractures, head injuries, chemical exposure)
Volume: ~400–600 customer incidents per year across 200 stores; ~90% minor (first aid only), ~10% requiring medical facility referral
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: First Aid Certified Staff, Customer Service Representative, LP Officer, Store Manager, Insurance Claims Coordinator, Legal Counsel, Safety Officer
Source: workflow W1266 — Store-Level Customer Safety Incident Management, First Aid Response &amp; Liability Documentation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1266_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1266_Lane1" name="First Aid Certified Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1266_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1266_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1266_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1266_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1266_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1266_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1266_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1266_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1266_Start4" name="Ad-hoc — triggered by any customer injury, illness, or safety incident occurring on…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1266_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1266_Task5" name="Immediate incident response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Immediate incident response: Upon witnessing or being alerted to a customer safety incident: (a) first responder (nearest staff member) ensures scene safety — stop any equipment, block hazard area, prevent additional injuries; (b) assess customer condition: (i) minor injury (small cut, bruise, minor slip) — provide first aid on-site, (ii) moderate injury (deep cut, possible fracture, head bump with confusion) — provide first aid and offer medical transport, (iii) severe injury (unconscious, severe bleeding, chest pain, seizure) — call emergency services (911 or local emergency number); (c) for all incidents: remain with customer, offer reassurance, do not move customer if spinal injury suspected
Responsible (R): First Aid Certified Staff / Nearest Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1266_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1266_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1266_Task6" name="First aid administration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: First aid administration: Trained staff administers first aid per store first aid protocol: (a) retrieve store first aid kit (located at customer service counter, receiving dock, and lumber yard); (b) for minor cuts: clean, disinfect, apply bandage; (c) for slips/falls: assess for fracture (swelling, deformity, inability to bear weight), apply ice pack, offer seat; (d) for chemical exposure (paint, solvent): flush affected area with water per SDS per W698, seek medical evaluation if eye exposure; (e) document first aid administered — time, type, items used from first aid kit; (f) restock first aid kit within 24 hours
Responsible (R): First Aid Certified Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1266_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1266_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1266_Task7" name="Incident documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Incident documentation: Store Manager completes incident documentation within 1 hour: (a) system incident report: (i) customer name, contact number, address, (ii) date, time, exact location in store (aisle, zone, fixture), (iii) description of incident (what happened, what caused the fall/injury), (iv) witness names and contact information, (v) CCTV timestamp for the incident (preserve footage per W838 — do not overwrite), (vi) first aid administered, (vii) customer disposition (walked away, transported to hospital, refused treatment); (b) photograph scene conditions (wet floor, fallen merchandise, tripping hazard); (c) customer statement (written or recorded with customer consent); (d) Store Manager assessment of contributing factors and immediate corrective action taken
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1266_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1266_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1266_Task8" name="Customer follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer follow-up: Within 24 hours: (a) Store Manager contacts customer to check on condition; (b) if customer visited hospital, obtain medical certificate and diagnosis; (c) if customer incurred medical expenses, offer to reimburse reasonable first aid/consultation costs per company policy (up to PHP 5,000 without Legal approval); (d) for incidents involving potential liability (moderate-to-severe injury): (i) notify Insurance Claims Coordinator per W285, (ii) notify Legal Counsel for documentation review, (iii) do not admit liability or make promises — express concern and support only; (e) document all follow-up communications in incident file
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Customer Service Representative
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1266_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1266_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1266_Task9" name="Corrective action &amp; preventive measures">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Corrective action &amp; preventive measures: Within 7 days: (a) Store Manager implements immediate corrective action: (i) repair or remove hazard (fix loose shelving, clean spill, replace broken floor tile), (ii) install additional warning signage, (iii) restrict customer access to hazardous area during operations; (b) if incident reveals systemic risk: (i) notify Safety Officer for assessment per W141, (ii) implement chain-wide corrective action if hazard exists at multiple stores (e.g., unsecured display shelving, inadequate forklift barriers), (iii) update store safety checklist; (c) for recurring incident patterns (same store, same location, same hazard): escalate to COO for capital investment (floor resurfacing, improved lighting, physical barriers)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Safety Officer
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 hours per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1266_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1266_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1266_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1266_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1266_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-313 (ensure controlled execution — Occupational Health &amp; Safety (PA-24.1).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1266_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1266_Annotation11" targetRef="W1266_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
