    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5504" name="W5504. Extreme-Heat Work Interruption &amp; Occupational Heat-Stress Management (DOLE Heat-Index Advisory Response)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Program establishment and annual pre-dry-season review; (b) PAGASA heat-index forecast or advisory reaching action thresholds for any store/DC locality — Extreme Caution 33–41°C, Danger 42–51°C, Extreme Danger 52°C and above; (c) heat-related illness symptom or incident at any site; (d) post-season review
Frequency: Pre-season readiness Jan–Feb; advisory-driven activations ~10–20 days/site/year in the hotter regions (fewer in Mindanao, more in Central Luzon and NCR), of which Danger-level episodes ~2–5 days/site/year; illness response rare (a handful of chain-wide cases per year)
Volume: ~205 sites (200 stores + 4 DCs) with ~6–10 outdoor-exposed roles per store (lumber yard per W438, garden center, receiving dock, parking and cart crews) and ~25–35 per DC (docks, yard, van loading) → ~1,300–2,100 employees directly exposed on a chain-wide Danger day, plus delivery and installation crews in non-air-conditioned vehicles (VS-06/VS-12)
Owner: Safety Officer
Participants: Store Manager, Assistant Store Manager, DC Manager, Department Supervisors, OH Nurse (VS-83), HR Manager (VS-19.3), Payroll (W10), Labor Relations (VS-84), Store Communication (VS-63), Regional Manager (VS-177), Maintenance (W47)
Source: workflow W5504 — Extreme-Heat Work Interruption &amp; Occupational Heat-Stress Management (DOLE Heat-Index Advisory Response)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5504_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5504_Lane1" name="Safety Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5504_Lane2" name="Store">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5504_Lane3" name="Department Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5504_Lane4" name="First Aider">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5504_Lane5" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5504_Lane6" name="HR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5504_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5504_Start8" name="(a) Program establishment and annual pre-dry-season review; (b) PAGASA heat-index…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5504_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5504_Task9" name="Threshold matrix">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Threshold matrix: HSE owns the Extreme-Heat Protocol mapping PAGASA heat-index categories to actions — Caution 27–32°C: standard hydration; Extreme Caution 33–41°C: water stations checked, paid 15-min rest break per 2 hours of outdoor work, outdoor tasks re-sequenced to shaded or cooler hours; Danger 42–51°C: non-essential outdoor tasks suspended, essential outdoor work (yard loading, dock work) on 30-min-per-2-hours work-rest cycling with indoor/outdoor rotation every 30–45 min; Extreme Danger 52°C and above: all outdoor work suspended, with the site head able to shorten outdoor-dependent service windows (lumber-yard loading) with Regional Manager concurrence (VS-177); aligned to DOLE occupational-safety guidance on heat stress and RA 11058/DO 252-25 duties; consulted with the union/employee representatives where a CBA exists (VS-84.1)
Responsible (R): Safety Officer
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 3–5 days initial; 1 day/year refresh</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5504_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5504_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5504_Task10" name="Pre-season readiness (Jan–Feb)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-season readiness (Jan–Feb): site risk mapping of yard, garden and dock exposure; equipment readiness — potable water stations, shaded or ventilated rest areas, industrial fans and misting at yard booths, cooling towels and ice packs in first-aid kits, electrolyte sachets stocked; acclimatization rule for new hires and returning workers (outdoor exposure ramped over ~14 days); supervisor training refresh on symptom recognition (W655); communications package pushed to sites (VS-63); readiness items folded into the W141 monthly inspection checklist for the season
Responsible (R): Safety Officer / Maintenance
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: ~0.5 day/site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5504_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5504_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5504_Task11" name="Daily monitoring and activation (Mar–May, extended per PAGASA)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Daily monitoring and activation (Mar–May, extended per PAGASA): each morning the site checks the locality heat-index forecast; on a threshold breach it activates the matrix and logs an activation record; HSE pushes chain-wide advisory days when broad advisories are issued; the day&#x27;s measures broadcast to supervisors through store communication (VS-63), noting any LGU or DOLE advisory alignment
Responsible (R): Store/DC Manager
Accountable (A): Safety Officer
Duration: 10–15 min/site on advisory days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5504_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5504_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5504_Task12" name="Work adjustment execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Work adjustment execution: supervisors re-sequence outdoor tasks (lumber loading, garden watering, container stuffing) to the 6–10 AM window, enforce the rest and hydration cycle, rotate roles, and run a buddy system for yard work in the Danger band with a designated cool-down area; customer vehicle loading assistance (W438) continues under rotation; delivery dispatch (VS-06) moves non-urgent bulky deliveries to early slots; installation jobs (VS-12) re-planned with customers
Responsible (R): Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: Continuous on affected days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5504_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5504_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5504_Task13" name="Symptom recognition and emergency response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Symptom recognition and emergency response: first-aid-trained staff respond to cramps and heat exhaustion (shade, active cooling, hydration, clinic referral per VS-83); suspected heatstroke is a medical emergency — emergency transport activated, OH Nurse informed, incident recorded per W140; serious cases feed DOLE-reportable OSH records (W436) and workers&#x27; compensation claims (W805)
Responsible (R): First Aider / OH Nurse
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: 1–4 hrs per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5504_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5504_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5504_Task14" name="Vulnerable-worker accommodation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Vulnerable-worker accommodation: pregnant employees, older workers, medically at-risk staff (per W804 surveillance) and non-acclimatized new hires receive priority reassignment to indoor or cooler roles for the season without loss of pay; HR tracks accommodations (VS-19.3); no employee is penalized for stopping work on a reasonable heat-illness belief (non-retaliation per the OSH policy)
Responsible (R): HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: As needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5504_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5504_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5504_Task15" name="Pay and timekeeping administration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Pay and timekeeping administration: a T&amp;A heat-interruption/adjustment code captures adjusted hours once an activation record exists; pay treatment follows the no-work-no-pay principle as modified by company policy and CBA (BuildRight policy pays scheduled shifts on company-initiated suspension under this protocol, subject to CFO/CHRO approval); Payroll mapping (W10) tested pre-season; Labor Relations (VS-84) consulted on disputes
Responsible (R): HR / Payroll
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hrs setup + exception handling</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5504_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5504_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5504_Task16" name="Records, review and integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Records, review and integration: activation log, symptom and incident records, and task-disruption cost captured per season; post-season review (June) updates the threshold matrix and equipment list; feeds the annual OSH program and WAIR/AMR reporting (W436), the BCP hazard annex (VS-26), climate scenario work (W5501), and ESG social metrics (VS-25)
Responsible (R): Safety Officer
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 day chain-wide post-season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5504_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5504_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5504_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5504_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5504_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-313 (ensure controlled execution — Occupational Health &amp; Safety (PA-24.1).) | - CTL-226 (ensure OHS compliance &amp; incident management.) | - operational: activation log reviewed monthly in season; rest-break compliance spot-checked on advisory days
Owner: Safety Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5504_Assoc19" sourceRef="W5504_Annotation18" targetRef="W5504_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
