    <bpmn:process id="W_W5549" name="W5549. Suicide Attempt / Self-Harm Incident Response &amp; Psychosocial-Aftermath Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A suicide attempt, act of self-harm, or death by suspected suicide occurs on BuildRight premises (store, DC, yard, or parking) involving a customer, employee, contractor, or visitor — including attempts discovered in progress
Frequency: Rare; the realistic chain-wide expectation is fewer than one event every several years; the aftermath protocol is exercised through the critical-incident drill rotation
Volume: 1 event × the immediate scene population plus directly-witnessing staff (typically 3–10 first-witness staff per event) × responders (EMS, PNP/SOCO where death is suspected)
Owner: Store Manager (site command during the event); HSE Manager (aftermath program owner)
Participants: Store Manager, trained first-aiders per W501, Security Guard (scene control), PNP (incl. SOCO where death is suspected), EMS, HR &amp; Occupational Health (W2865 counseling/EAP), VP Legal, Corporate Communications (single-spokesperson protocol), CHRO, DOLE reporting chain where an employee is involved (W140/W436), barangay crisis responders where engaged
Source: workflow W5549 — Suicide Attempt / Self-Harm Incident Response &amp; Psychosocial-Aftermath Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5549_LaneSet9">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5549_Lane1" name="First Aider">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_Start10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5549_Lane2" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5549_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5549_Lane4" name="Duty Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5549_Lane5" name="Corporate Communications">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5549_Lane6" name="HR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5549_Lane7" name="HSE Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5549_Lane8" name="HSE">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5549_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5549_Start10" name="A suicide attempt, act of self-harm, or death by suspected suicide occurs on BuildRight…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5549_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5549_Task11" name="Immediate response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Immediate response: render aid per W501 immediately (EMS 911); clear onlookers and create privacy screens (fixture covers, aisle closure); assign one staff member to meet EMS at the entrance; do not delay aid for scene-perfection — aid first, preservation second
Responsible (R): First Aider / Duty Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5549_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5549_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5549_Task12" name="Scene preservation &amp; police handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Scene preservation &amp; police handoff: where death is suspected (or uncertain), treat the area as a potential crime scene — nothing moved or removed beyond what aid required, staff rotated out of the scene, PNP called; SOCO processes the scene; store provides CCTV preservation request per the W471 evidence chain
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Until PNP release</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5549_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5549_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5549_Task13" name="Trading decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Trading decision: section-off the affected area vs. full temporary closure — decision by Store Manager with Regional Manager consult, factoring scene extent, police direction, and staff readiness; if trading continues, the scene area stays closed and screened; no re-staffing of directly-witnessing employees at the scene zone same-day
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: &lt; 1 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5549_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5549_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5549_Task14" name="Witness &amp; staff immediate care">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Witness &amp; staff immediate care: directly-witnessing staff removed from duty with pay; psychological first aid by trained peers/managers (listen, do not probe); EAP counseling activated per W2865 with same-day access; a named HR contact assigned to each affected employee; no statements to anyone except police, HR, or Legal
Responsible (R): Duty Supervisors / HR
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5549_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5549_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5549_Task15" name="Communication protocol">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Communication protocol: single-spokesperson rule (Corporate Communications) — a no-comment-until-facts script for media and social; no details in any internal channel beyond operational need-to-know; no cause characterization anywhere in writing; if the person involved is an employee, family contact is made by a designated senior HR/Legal pair, in person where possible, never by phone script
Responsible (R): Corporate Communications / HR
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5549_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5549_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5549_Task16" name="Employee-victim branch">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Employee-victim branch (if the person involved is an employee): hospital liaison and family single-point contact; DOLE 24-hour notification where the event is work-related per W140/W436 with facts only (no cause speculation in any report); employment-status, benefits, and medical-leave handling per W805/W2850-class chains; confidentiality maintained — mental-health information is sensitive personal information under the privacy canon
Responsible (R): HR / HSE
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Days–weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5549_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5549_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5549_Task17" name="Aftermath program">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Aftermath program: structured staff debrief within 72 hours by a trained facilitator (external CISM resource where internal capacity is thin); ongoing counseling access monitored; duty-roster changes for scene-zone staff; site walk-through after PNP release to restore and review the area (a standard means-restriction and access review of the site — heights, enclosed or secluded zones — as prudent practice); union/employee-representative coordination where applicable
Responsible (R): HSE Manager / HR
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5549_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5549_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5549_Task18" name="Documentation &amp; review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Documentation &amp; review: incident record per W140 with a sensitive-handling flag (access-restricted; no cause speculation); the comms log archived; after-action review of the response (timing, script adherence, care coverage) feeding the critical-incident drill rotation; no disciplinary or policy conclusions drawn except from the verified facts
Responsible (R): HSE / HR / VP Legal
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk (review sign-off)
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5549_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5549_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5549_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5549_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5549_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-226 (ensure OHS compliance &amp; incident management.) | - operational: no statement on the event&#x27;s nature or cause is made or recorded by any function other than the single spokesperson and, for employees, the HR/Legal family pair | - operational: directly-witnessing staff are stood down same-day with pay and offered counseling access within 24 hours — both logged
Owner: Store Manager (site command during the event); HSE Manager (aftermath program owner)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5549_Assoc21" sourceRef="W5549_Annotation20" targetRef="W5549_Start10" associationDirection="None" />
