    <bpmn:process id="W_W5552" name="W5552. DOLE Imminent-Danger Work-Stoppage Order Response, Abatement &amp; Reinstatement Gate" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: DOLE issues a work-stoppage or work-suspension order on an imminent-danger finding under RA 11058 and its IRR (DO 198-18 class) — covering a BuildRight store, DC, or a specific operation within a site (e.g., lumber-yard crane, paint-mixing room, racking, mezzanine storage) — halting the affected operations until the danger is abated and DOLE clears resumption
Frequency: Rare; fewer than one order per several years chain-wide; the abatement discipline is exercised through the W512 safety-committee drill rotation
Volume: 1 event × the ordered scope (one operation to an entire site) × affected workers (10–40 per store operation; 40–120 at a DC) × the trading-continuity surface (partial closure per W850; full closure rides the E-02 custody chain if site-wide)
Owner: HSE Manager
Participants: Safety Officer (site), Store Manager / DC Operations Manager, Maintenance Staff (W240/W47), Regional Manager, HR Business Partner (worker redeployment &amp; pay continuity), Regulatory Compliance Officer (W506 calendar), VP Store Operations, DOLE Regional Office, Labor Relations Director where workers are covered (W2880)
Source: workflow W5552 — DOLE Imminent-Danger Work-Stoppage Order Response, Abatement &amp; Reinstatement Gate</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5552_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5552_Lane1" name="Safety Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5552_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5552_Lane3" name="HR Business Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5552_Lane4" name="Maintenance Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5552_Lane5" name="Regulatory Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5552_Lane6" name="HSE Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5552_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5552_Start8" name="DOLE issues a work-stoppage or work-suspension order on an imminent-danger finding under…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5552_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5552_Task9" name="Order receipt &amp; scope confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Order receipt &amp; scope confirmation: obtain the written order (or its written same-day confirmation where issued orally at inspection); confirm the exact scope — operations, areas, equipment — effective time and resumption conditions; register it in the W506 compliance calendar
Responsible (R): Safety Officer / Regulatory Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): HSE Manager
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5552_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5552_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5552_Task10" name="Immediate compliance &amp; area control">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Immediate compliance &amp; area control: halt the ordered operations with no partial trading of the affected zone; barricade and lockout/tag-out affected equipment; post the order at the site; remove workers from the danger area
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Safety Officer / Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager (store) / DC Operations Manager (DC)
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5552_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5552_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5552_Task11" name="Worker redeployment &amp; wage continuity">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Worker redeployment &amp; wage continuity: redeploy affected workers to unaffected duties where feasible; pay continuity for stoppage-affected workers per the OSH no-wage-loss rule; no forced leave and no retaliation — RA 11058 attaches penalties to retaliation
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / Store Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5552_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5552_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5552_Task12" name="Abatement program">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Abatement program: engineering/administrative fixes per the order&#x27;s findings (structural, guarding, ventilation, electrical) via the W240/W47 maintenance chains or an external engineer on the W1450-class assessment pattern; interim controls documented; photographic and works evidence retained for the lifting case
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff / Facilities / Safety Officer
Accountable (A): HSE Manager
Duration: Per order (days–weeks)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5552_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5552_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5552_Task13" name="Contest/clarification posture (where warranted)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Contest/clarification posture (where warranted): request clarification or reconsideration of scope through the Regulatory Compliance Officer with VP Legal — comply first, contest second (the W5545 posture); no unilateral resumption while a contest runs
Responsible (R): Regulatory Compliance Officer / VP Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5552_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5552_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5552_Task14" name="DOLE re-inspection &amp; written lifting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: DOLE re-inspection &amp; written lifting: request re-inspection on abatement completion; resumption only after DOLE&#x27;s written lifting/clearance — never on internal judgment alone (the E-25 reopen-gate rule)
Responsible (R): HSE Manager / Safety Officer
Accountable (A): HSE Manager
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5552_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5552_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5552_Task15" name="Resumption &amp; verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Resumption &amp; verification: reopening mechanics per W850 (E-02 chain if site-wide); worker re-induction on the corrected hazards through the W512 safety-committee briefing; trading restored with monitoring through any ordered observation period
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Safety Officer / HR Business Partner
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5552_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5552_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5552_Task16" name="Register, drill &amp; chain-wide sweep">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Register, drill &amp; chain-wide sweep: record event, root cause and abatement evidence in the OSH learning register (W140-class); feed the W512 drill rotation; sweep the same defect class across all ~205 sites (the W5545 chain-wide defect-sweep pattern)
Responsible (R): HSE Manager / Safety Officer
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk (review sign-off)
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5552_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5552_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5552_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5552_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5552_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-313 (ensure controlled execution — Occupational Health &amp; Safety (PA-24.1).) | - CTL-226 (ensure OHS compliance &amp; incident management.) | - operational: no resumption without the written DOLE lifting order filed in the compliance calendar; wage continuity for stoppage-affected workers verified by payroll exception report through the order&#x27;s life
Owner: HSE Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5552_Assoc19" sourceRef="W5552_Annotation18" targetRef="W5552_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5552_Flow20" sourceRef="W5552_Start8" targetRef="W5552_Task9" />
